# ── Node / npm ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reinstalled from package-lock.json by `npm ci`. Platform-specific binary
# subpackages (esbuild, sharp, etc.) live inside, so committing this would
# break cross-platform CI + collaborators on different OSes.
node_modules/

# Logs from failed installs / runs.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Local npm/yarn/pnpm caches (rare at the repo root but possible).
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnpm-store/

# TypeScript incremental-build cache. Regenerated on every `tsc -b`.
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both packages compile to dist/ — api via tsc, frontend via vite build.
# CI regenerates these; committing them creates merge conflicts on every
# build.
dist/
build/

# Vite's dev-server cache.
.vite/

# Test coverage reports.
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ── Secrets / local environment ────────────────────────────────
# .env holds JWT_SECRET, CREDENTIALS_MASTER_KEY, DB passwords, the Discord
# webhook URL, etc. NEVER commit. .env.example IS committed (with
# placeholder values) so newcomers know which keys to fill in.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.development

# ── Docker / runtime state ─────────────────────────────────────
# Redis writes a dump.rdb to ./redis/ every 60s when there's been a change.
# Dev runtime state — do not commit. If you want a known baseline dump for
# testing, save it elsewhere and `cp` it into ./redis/ on `down -v`.
redis/dump.rdb
redis/appendonly.aof
redis/appendonlydir/

# Postgres data lives in a named docker volume (`postgres_data`), not on
# disk. If anyone ever bind-mounts it to ./postgres/, ignore that too.
postgres/
pgdata/

# ── Workflows folder ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The api bind-mounts ./workflows/ as a runtime store. Each workflow folder
# can hold a `.history/` of snapshots produced by snapshotWorkflow() and
# `.staging/` for AI-driven edits. Both are local state — keep the workflow
# *definitions* (params.json, workflow.json, SKILL.md, icons) committable
# but ignore the per-folder mutable subdirs.
workflows/*/.history/
workflows/*/.staging/

# ── IDE / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*.bak
*.orig
*~

# Per-user JetBrains config sometimes leaks here.
*.iml
.idea_modules/

# ── OS-generated files ─────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
Icon$'\r'

# ── CI / release artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────
# Tarballs the release workflow stages before uploading to the GitHub
# release. They're outputs, not source.
coffee-maker-*-deploy.tar.gz
coffee-maker-*-bundle.tar.gz
out/

# `docker save` output used to hand-carry built images to offline hosts —
# build output, never commit (hundreds of MB). Replaces the old
# rdp-sidecar/*.tar rule now that images are saved per-service.
api/*.tar
frontend/*.tar

# ── Misc ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ad-hoc local notes — useful during exploration, not for the repo.
NOTES.md
TODO.md
scratch/

# Vite ssr-manifest and any generated public asset directories that some
# plugins drop here.
**/ssr-manifest.json

redis/
/workflows/
references/
data/

.history/
workflow-studio/